  "text": "```python\nfrom typing import List, Tuple\n\n\ndef merge_intervals(intervals: List[Tuple[int, int]]) -> List[Tuple[int, int]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Merge overlapping intervals.\n    \n    Given a list of intervals represented as tuples (start, end), this function\n    merges all overlapping intervals and returns a new list of non-overlapping\n    intervals.\n    \n    Args:\n        intervals: A list of tuples, where each tuple represents an interval\n                   with (start, end) where start <= end.\n    \n    Returns:\n        A list of merged, non-overlapping intervals sorted by start time.\n    \n    Raises:\n        ValueError: If any interval has start > end.\n        TypeError: If intervals is not a list or contains invalid types.\n    \n    Example:\n        >>> merge_intervals([(1, 3), (2, 6), (8, 10), (15, 18)])\n        [(1, 6), (8, 10), (15, 18)]\n        \n        >>> merge_intervals([(1, 4), (4, 5)])\n        [(1, 5)]\n        \n        >>> merge_intervals",
